  "priorBroadScope": "448 passing publication, egress, action and Supabase tests. Precedes final route/issuer terminal-denial additions and final test type annotation. Current137-test receipt and follow-ups, not that earlier broad run, bind the final Supabase correction. Final whole-source CI remains required.",
  "defects": [
    "Raw/fabricated actors reached credential and provider paths. All exported provisioning operations now require the original actor, with exact owner checks before user-selectable canonical reads or writes.",
    "Source revisions/tombstones and full metadata were not retained across provider waits. The original owner-scoped six-component source epoch now gates every management/storage read and native write.",
    "Private-key discovery did not verify selected provider-project membership. It now requires the exact ref on the original token-owned provider account.",
    "Schema and bucket writes ran on connection alone. They now require the existing durable confirmation, managed-vault producer attestation, exact one-use permit, central egress decision and persisted audit before effects.",
    "Native direct SQL disabled peer verification, used a wrong direct host and retried authentication/query failures. TLS peer verification is required, hosts are fixed issuer destinations, only pre-query connectivity failures can recover, and authorization/certificate/query denial stops the sequence.",
    "Failed or uncertain management dispatch previously fell through to password SQL/storage. Approved execution now uses one selected method with no security or uncertain-outcome fallback.",
    "Provider key name anon could override an explicit secret type. Explicit type wins, private/public prefixes cannot swap roles, and old malformed public bundles are denied without deleting credentials.",
    "The generic credential floor missed Supabase secret-key prefixes under neutral fields. It now raises those values to CREDENTIAL_SECRET. Publishable values remain public. No policy exception was added.",
    "Pipeline and OAuth catches hid issuer, source or ownership denial. Those denials now stop the relevant caller instead of continuing fallback or unrelated env export."
  ],
  "authority": "Existing businessAction confirmation, claim/consume/finish and authority kernel only. This is a native adapter extension, not a new scheduler, ledger, issuer or security framework.",
  "data": "Only fixed owned-provider metadata and canonical static SQL. Credentials stay in existing server vault/auth channels. No customer records, raw keys, plan proof or provider errors enter model/client/audit output. SQL and exact private bucket definitions are visible in the confirmation.",
  "verification": "Provider/PG protocols and original confirmation/vault code run against synthetic fixtures. SQL completion requires a separate four-table/RLS metadata query and private storage readback. Positive PG scenarios assert actual client TLS configuration, not a live Supabase handshake. No live provisioning, SQL, credentials or account resources were accessed.",
  "quota": "No model or paid provider execution, no extra infrastructure. Existing control-plane operations are finite: one selected static SQL sequence, one schema metadata probe and at most two private empty bucket creates. Native action authority and one-use receipts are required.",
  "upstream": "Actual authenticated OAuth/manual routes, original pipeline actor/signal, one-click CAS and manual vault connections are traced and tested. Raw project-creation POST807 and shared GitHub/Composio/research callers remain independent unresolved obligations. No whole-file or upstream promotion.",
  "testContractContinuation": "Legacy direct-write fixture cases now invoke real native confirmations or assert no write without them. The original 200/409 x private/public postcondition combinations and partial schema/RLS/storage failures remain in the canonical authority suite. No skips or frozen criteria changed.",
